ogram (E-Rate) to purchase discounted Wi-Fi hotspots and associated mobile connectivity service for off-premises use by students, school staff, and library patrons. Under the rule, E-Rate participants must implement acceptable use policies that require hotspots to be used primarily for educational purposes. &nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-02-06T13:51:23Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"A joint resolution providing for congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the Federal Communications Commission relating to \"Addressing the Homework Gap Through the E-Rate Program\".","type":"sjres","updateDate":"2026-09-08T18:03:40Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-08T18:09:52Z"}
